course: dictionary
lesson: 12962
title: Excursion: a trip with a purpose
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An excursion is a short trip, often with a group, to visit a place for fun or to learn, and then come back. Look at the clues in this sentence: «Our class went on an excursion to the science museum on Friday.» Class, museum and Friday all tell you it is a trip out, with a group, and you will return the same day.
explain: Check the word by swapping in your meaning. «Please bring a packed lunch for the excursion to the farm.» Put in trip instead: «Please bring a packed lunch for the trip to the farm.» It still makes sense, so trip is a good meaning for excursion here.
explain: Words can change from place to place. An Aussie teacher says, «Permission slips for Thursday's excursion are due back.» In Australia and New Zealand, an excursion is a school trip. In the UK people say school trip, and in the US they say field trip. When you are not sure, a dictionary will help.
fact: An excursion is a short trip, often with a group, to visit a place for fun or to learn.
fact: «We went on an excursion to the zoo.» Here excursion is a noun, a trip you take and then return from.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, an excursion is a school trip, so «The excursion is on Monday» means the school trip is on Monday.
fact: Other words for the same idea in other places: school trip (UK) and field trip (US).
fact: Excursion often comes with phrases like «go on an excursion», «a day excursion» and «class excursion».
exercise: «The excursion to the zoo was on Monday.» What is an excursion? | A long journey by plane to another country | * A short trip with a group, often to learn or have fun | A zoo animal that is very big
exercise: Maya says, «Our class excursion is on Friday.» What does excursion mean here? | * A school trip out to learn or have fun | A lesson about maths | A quiet day in the classroom with no visitors | A test for the whole class
exercise: Which sentence uses excursion correctly? | I read an excursion before bed. | She cooked an excursion for tea. | * We went on a class excursion to the farm and fed the goats. | The excursion was very tall and green.
test: «The bus cost for our excursion was 40 pounds for the class.» In maths, what might you work out from this? | The colour of the bus | * The cost for each pupil, or how many buses are needed | How many words are in the sentence
test: An Aussie friend says, «Our excursion to the beach is next week.» What would a UK child call this? | A holiday abroad | * A school trip is the UK name, so the answer is a school trip | A school dinner | A school trip
exam: Which word means the same as excursion in «We are going on a day excursion to the museum»? | Holiday | Test | * Trip | Lesson
